// @@@ For every index i that is greater than or equal to 0 and less than the current index, the element at this index in the list is equal to the element at the same index in the old list. If the element at the current index is null in both the new and old list, the element at the same index in the old list is also null.

--------------------
// @@@ For any index 'i' in the list, if the index is not less than 0 and not greater than or equal to the size of the list, the element at that index in the list remains the same as the element at that index in the old list. If the element at the index in the old list is null, so is the element at the index in the new list. Otherwise, the element at the index in the new list is equal to the element at the index in the old list.

--------------------
// @@@ For any index 'i' such that 0 <= i < index, the element at position 'i' in the list is either null in both the old and new list or equals to the old list's element at position 'i'.

